partialText:
&lt;p&gt;I worked on an analytics product with about sixteen charts: survival curves, forest plots, histograms and scatter plots. Our charting library had not published a release in over a year. Nothing was broken, but I was worried about future React upgrades and who would maintain it. I wanted to know what we could move to.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I took two charts from the product, a survival curve and a scatter plot, and built each with nivo, Recharts, ECharts, visx, TanStack Charts and Chart.js. I also built them in React with hand-written SVG. All seven implementations followed the same spec and used the same synthetic data, with animation off.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At typical sizes (three survival series with 200 points each, and a 500-point scatter) the native-speed timings gave me no clear winner. Within each chart type, all seven were less than one frame apart.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At 10,000 scatter points, the median mount times spread out: 24 ms for hand-written SVG, 33 ms for visx, 53 ms for TanStack Charts, 80–86 ms for Chart.js and ECharts, 310 ms for Recharts and 3.2 seconds for nivo's SVG scatter. Both Canvas implementations took longer than my hand-written SVG. nivo also has a Canvas scatter renderer; I did not test it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Those are measurements from headless Chromium on my M3 Pro with other work running. They helped narrow my choices for these two chart types. I also compared how much code each implementation needed and how much JavaScript it loaded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How I measured
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every comparison I found was a feature checklist or one &lt;code&gt;console.time&lt;/code&gt; around a render. I wanted numbers I could defend in a design review. Getting them took more work on the stopwatch than on the charts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What was tested
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The survival curve has step lines, a shaded confidence band per series, small ticks for censored observations, and a tooltip with every series' value at the pointer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The scatter plot has circles sized per point and coloured per group, with a nearest-point tooltip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The versions were nivo 0.99, Recharts 3.10, ECharts 6.1, visx 4.0, TanStack Charts 1.2 and Chart.js 4.6. The hand-written version uses React and SVG with no d3. All seven were written against &lt;a href="https://github.com/GusevP/chart-bench/blob/main/apps/bench/ARMS.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;one spec&lt;/a&gt;: same size, same marks, same tooltip content. Each library was used the way its docs recommend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every implementation gets byte-identical data from a seeded generator, at two sizes. Typical is 3 series × 200 points and 500 scatter points. Heavy is 6 series × 1,000 points and 10,000 scatter points.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each cell is one warm-up load and nine measured page loads of a production build in headless Chromium, reported as the median. I ran everything twice: at native speed, and with Chrome's 4× CPU slowdown, to make the differences easier to see.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I ran this on a busy laptop, with the libraries in a fixed order while the load changed, and I have no measured noise figure. The comparison against an earlier, quieter run is in &lt;a href="https://github.com/GusevP/chart-bench/blob/main/apps/bench/results/report.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;report.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My rule of thumb: call it a tie if the gap is under one frame, or if a heavy-chart result took less than 20% longer than the faster one. That cutoff is my judgement, not a measurement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The stopwatch
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The instrument is a small package, &lt;a href="https://github.com/GusevP/chart-bench/blob/main/packages/bench-stage/src/BenchStage.tsx" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bench-stage&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Its core:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestSettle&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestedRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestedRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;mark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bench:settled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;measure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bench:mount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bench:start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bench:settled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I measured it this way:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chart is not rendered on page load. The runner starts the clock when it mounts the chart, after page startup and module evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The clock stops two animation frames after the chart reports done. The first callback runs after React's commit, the second after the browser has produced a frame with the chart in it. The harness does not watch pixels reach the screen; this is a convention, applied to every library in the same way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SVG and Canvas report "done" differently and then stop the clock the same way. An SVG chart is done when React commits. A Canvas chart is done when the library says it has drawn: ECharts' &lt;code&gt;finished&lt;/code&gt; event, or a Chart.js plugin's &lt;code&gt;afterRender&lt;/code&gt;. Both then go through the same double &lt;code&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/code&gt;. Marking straight from the Canvas callback would have given every Canvas library a free frame.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reason for waiting is that React's commit is not the end of the work. Recharts' first commit put 2 of the chart's 30,109 DOM nodes in the page; the rest arrived about 295 ms later, before any frame was drawn. A timer stopped at the commit would have missed almost all of it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The price of this timer is that it counts in frames. An empty page with no chart measures 22–26 ms, so anything less than one frame (16.7 ms) apart is a tie.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Results
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Full tables for both speeds are in &lt;a href="https://github.com/GusevP/chart-bench/blob/main/apps/bench/results/report.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;report.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Mount time with the 4× CPU slowdown (median ms, empty page ≈ 21–25 ms)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;library&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;survival typical&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;survival heavy&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;scatter typical&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;scatter heavy&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;no library&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21.3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;27.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;23.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;103.6&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;visx&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;22.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;51.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21.3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;127.9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TanStack Charts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;20.9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;90.6&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;20.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;195.9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Chart.js&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;32.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;60.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;36.8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;318.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;ECharts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;49.2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;123.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;48.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;260.9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;nivo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;62.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;149.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;134.8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;14,899.8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recharts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;103.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;446.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;111.7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,195.8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the typical columns, hand-written SVG, visx and TanStack are one group. Recharts and nivo's scatter sit well above it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the heavy scatter, visx took 23% longer than plain SVG and Chart.js took 22% longer than ECharts. Both are just past my 20% line, and in an earlier run the same day both pairs were inside it, so I call them ties.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the heavy survival chart plain SVG has the lowest median, but two of its nine runs landed at 53–55 ms, inside visx's range. I don't count that as a clean lead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At native speed, the typical timings for each chart were all less than one frame apart: 19–29 ms for the survival chart and 22–37 ms for the scatter. For these two charts at typical sizes, that is too close for me to rank.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The 10,000-point scatter did separate them: 24 ms with hand-written SVG, 33 ms with visx, 53 ms with TanStack, 80–86 ms with the two Canvas libraries, 310 ms with Recharts and 3.2 s with nivo. That is nivo's SVG scatter with animation off; nivo also ships a Canvas scatter, which I did not test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Canvas did not win at 10,000 points. The ECharts and Chart.js implementations mounted about twice as slowly as visx and plain SVG, or worse, at both CPU speeds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Hover (median of each sweep's longest frame, 4× slowdown)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pointer sweeps the chart in 60 steps and the harness records the longest frame of each sweep. Most cells are one frame. On the 10,000-point scatter Recharts takes 133 ms (8 frames), Chart.js and visx 50 ms, plain SVG and TanStack 33 ms. nivo and ECharts stay at one frame; nivo hit-tests against a precomputed Voronoi mesh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Weight and code
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;library&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;library cost (gzip)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;code tokens for both charts&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;DOM nodes, 10k scatter&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;no library&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2.2 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3,134&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10,075&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;visx&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;25.0 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,683&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10,117&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Chart.js&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;55.6 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,214&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2 (canvas)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TanStack Charts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;56.8 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;720&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10,055&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;nivo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;103.1 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;993&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;10,094&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recharts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;106.2 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,064&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;30,109&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;ECharts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;164.2 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,117&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5 (canvas)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Library cost is the gzipped JS a page loads, minus the same page with no chart library. It is the cost of these implementations and their imports. TanStack's figure includes about 15 KB for its &lt;code&gt;motion&lt;/code&gt; renderer, which only the playground's effects mode uses but the timed pages still load.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Code tokens count both charts with their tooltips, after TypeScript turns the code into plain JS, without imports, comments or whitespace. The no-library count overstates what those two charts need, because it includes shared axis code for the playground's other charts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What each library made me do
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;nivo.&lt;/strong&gt; Bands and censoring ticks had to be custom layers. The linear scale is &lt;code&gt;nice&lt;/code&gt; by default and quietly stretched my x axis from 412 to 450. Slices only group points with exactly the same x, so the survival tooltip became my own lookup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recharts.&lt;/strong&gt; Survival data had to be reshaped into one row per x and forward-filled. Skip that and the shared tooltip silently drops any series with no point at that exact x. Animation has to be switched off on every element separately. It renders three DOM nodes per scatter point.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ECharts.&lt;/strong&gt; A misspelled top-level option key type-checks cleanly, because the option type has an index signature, and then throws inside &lt;code&gt;setOption&lt;/code&gt;. Misspelled nested keys are just ignored.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;visx.&lt;/strong&gt; Everything is composed from primitives, and the hit-testing is your own code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TanStack Charts 1.2.&lt;/strong&gt; A mark grammar in the Observable Plot tradition. Censoring ticks are a stock &lt;code&gt;tickX&lt;/code&gt;, and the band is &lt;code&gt;areaY&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;y1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;y2&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;marks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;decorative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;areaY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;y1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;lower&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;y2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;upper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fillOpacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;curve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stepAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;lineY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;curve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stepAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;decorative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;tickX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;censored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chart.js.&lt;/strong&gt; Almost everything is native, including censoring ticks as a rotated &lt;code&gt;pointStyle: 'line'&lt;/code&gt;. Watch the naming: &lt;code&gt;stepped: 'before'&lt;/code&gt; is what d3 calls step-after. The survival tooltip needed a custom interaction mode.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I would pick
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For another app with these two chart types, this is my shortlist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the goal is less code, I would prototype TanStack Charts first: 720 tokens, and nearly every requirement was a stock mark. Its &lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tanstack/charts?activeTab=versions" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;first npm release&lt;/a&gt; was on 29 July 2026, so the risk is its age.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the goal is control and a small bundle, I would take visx, or no library at all. They were the two fastest on the big scatter and the smallest. The cost is code: 1,683 tokens with visx and 3,134 with nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would not put a large scatter on nivo's SVG renderer. 10,000 points took 3.2 s, and &lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@nivo/core?activeTab=versions" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;its last npm release&lt;/a&gt;, 0.99.0, was on 23 May 2025.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With Recharts I would check two things before committing. The survival tooltip needs a data reshape that fails silently if you forget it. And in the stress cases here it was the slowest library on the heavy survival chart and the worst on hover at 10,000 points.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And if you benchmark charts yourself: stop the clock after the browser has drawn the chart, and send SVG and Canvas through the same last step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One machine, one browser engine, headless, and the machine was busy. The libraries always ran in the same order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two chart types. A product full of bar charts or dual axes could rank differently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code tokens measure what this spec needed, written the way each library's docs suggest. Someone who knows one library well might need fewer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hover is a scripted sweep and not real input latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/GusevP/chart-bench" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;The repository&lt;/a&gt; has the harness, all seven ports, the raw data for every run and the scripts that build these tables. There is also a &lt;a href="https://gusevp.github.io/chart-bench/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;playground&lt;/a&gt;: paste your own data as JSON, pick the libraries, and it measures each one alone with a fresh page load per run, across twelve chart types.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Forms are where a polished product can suddenly feel unreliable. A user submits an email, the button spins, and then… nothing useful happens. Maybe the request is still running. Maybe the server rejected the address. Maybe the response succeeded but the UI forgot to move on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React, this often starts with a harmless-looking &lt;code&gt;isLoading&lt;/code&gt; boolean. Over time it becomes a bucket for validation, network work, success messages, retries, and failures. The component still works, but it is hard to explain and harder to recover.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The better approach is to give the form a small, explicit async state model. It makes the JavaScript easier to reason about, and it gives users a clearer product experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why one loading boolean is not enough
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider this common shape:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setIsLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It looks simple until you ask a few questions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Should a second submit be blocked while client validation runs?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can the user edit the field after a server error?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does an old response still have permission to overwrite a newer attempt?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What should the button say after success?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The boolean answers only one question: some work is happening. It does not say what work, for which attempt, or what action is safe next. That missing context is where confusing UI come from.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Model the form as explicit async states
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a small email form, a useful model might be:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;idle -&amp;gt; validating -&amp;gt; submitting -&amp;gt; succeeded
  |         |             |
  +------ failed &amp;lt;---------+
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The exact names are less important than the transitions. A user can edit an &lt;code&gt;idle&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;failed&lt;/code&gt; form. A &lt;code&gt;submitting&lt;/code&gt; form can disable its submit action. A &lt;code&gt;succeeded&lt;/code&gt; form can show the next step instead of leaving a spinner on screen forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is not a reason to install a state-machine library for every input. A string plus a small reducer is often enough. The key is that impossible combinations become harder to create, like showing “Try again” while the request is still pending.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A small React implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a compact reducer for a form that requests an email verification message:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;initialState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;formReducer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;switch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;edit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;submit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;submitting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;succeeded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Check your inbox.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;failure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;requestId&lt;/code&gt; is doing quiet but important work. If a user submits twice, a slower old response cannot replace the result of the newer attempt. Race conditions are less visible on a fast local connection, then become real in production. This little guard save a lot of head scratching.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component can now render from &lt;code&gt;status&lt;/code&gt; instead of combining several loosely related booleans:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSubmitting&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;submitting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;canSubmit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSubmitting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;canSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSubmitting&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Sending…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Send verification email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The UI becomes more honest: the button communicates the current action, and the message has a stable place for assistive technology to discover it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Keep validation and server state separate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client validation and server failure are different kinds of feedback. “Enter a valid email” is actionable before a request. “This address is already registered” comes from the server. They should not compete for one generic &lt;code&gt;error&lt;/code&gt; string.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I usually keep a small field error beside the async status:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fieldError&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Check the email format.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then the submit handler exits before dispatching &lt;code&gt;submit&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;fieldError&lt;/code&gt; exists. The server response can focus on what the user should do next. This division also makes tests much more direct.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For test fixtures, use a recognizable but non-sensitive value, even when the case is about a temporary inbox. A label such as &lt;code&gt;fake e mail com&lt;/code&gt; can be kept as plain test data, but it should not become a misleading link or a real user-facing example. A small contract around email probes is useful too; see &lt;a href="https://dev.to/mrdapperx/ai-agent-email-probes-need-a-test-contract-bb0"&gt;a test contract for email probes&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Test transitions, not just screenshots
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Testing Library tests are more valuable when they follow the user journey:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Render the idle form.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit an invalid value and verify no request starts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit a valid value and verify the pending label.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve the request and verify the success message.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reject a later request and verify retry remains possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also test the stale-response case. Start request A, start request B, resolve A last, and assert that B's state remains visible. It feels slightly fussy, but this is exactly the bug that hides behind “works on my machine”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same thinking applies outside the browser. A release notification should have a clear contract about when it is emitted and what evidence it carries; &lt;a href="https://dev.to/jasonmills94/kubernetes-release-emails-as-a-cicd-gate-4c76"&gt;treating release emails as a CI/CD gate&lt;/a&gt; is a useful example of making that boundary explicit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Q&amp;amp;A: practical tradeoffs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Do I need a reducer for every form?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. For a one-field form with no retry or race risk, local state is fine. Use a reducer when several events update related state or when the allowed transitions matter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Should success be a permanent state?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Usually not. It can be a short-lived confirmation before navigation, or it can stay until the user edits the field. Choose the behavior that makes the next action obvious.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Is this overengineering?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It can be if the form has one synchronous action. For forms that send email, save data, or trigger payments, explicit states are cheaper than debugging a vague spinner later. The code is a little more words, but the product is less mysterious.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The main idea is simple: name the state your user is actually in. React then becomes the renderer of a clear contract, instead of a place where loading flags quietly accumulate. That shift makes features easier to ship, easier to test, and much nicer to recover from when the network does its usual weird stuff.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every hostel student at my university wakes up to the same question: &lt;em&gt;what's the mess serving, and is it worth walking down for?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The "official" answer was a PDF that nobody kept up to date. So I built the thing I actually wanted — a fast page that tells you today's food, with serving times, and lets students rate each meal so you know what you're walking into.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;👉 &lt;strong&gt;Live:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://nustmessmenu.oddmancy.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://nustmessmenu.oddmancy.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Today&lt;/strong&gt; — breakfast, lunch and dinner with serving timings, at a glance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;This week&lt;/strong&gt; — the full weekly menu so you can plan around the good days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ratings &amp;amp; reviews&lt;/strong&gt; — students rate each meal, so "chicken karahi" with a 4.5 reads very differently from one with a 1.8.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No login. No ads. Free.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deliberately boring, because boring is reliable:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React + TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; on the frontend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cloudflare Workers&lt;/strong&gt; serving it from the edge — cheap, globally fast, and it shrugs off traffic spikes (which mattered more than I expected — more on that another day).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A small backend&lt;/strong&gt; for the menu + review data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tailwind&lt;/strong&gt; for styling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SEO done properly&lt;/strong&gt;: server-rendered content, a real sitemap, and structured data — so when someone searches the mess menu, the site actually shows up instead of a stale link.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The engineering here is trivial. The part that made it &lt;em&gt;stick&lt;/em&gt; was removing exactly one daily friction for a few thousand people. The ratings turned a lookup tool into something students check &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; contribute to — that loop is what keeps it alive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're building something small, that's the bar worth aiming for: not "impressive," just "used every single day."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're a student (or just curious how the edge setup feels), take a look and leave a review on today's meals:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://nustmessmenu.oddmancy.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://nustmessmenu.oddmancy.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Happy to go deep on the Cloudflare Workers + SEO setup in the comments if anyone's interested.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shipping an e-commerce storefront inside a Telegram Mini App using Next.js App Router seems straightforward until untrusted client state compromises your checkout process. Front-end developers frequently rely on &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; to identify the user and send cart totals directly from the client to an API route. Because &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; can be mutated by anyone opening your app in a standard browser or using browser developer tools, accepting unverified user IDs or total prices from the front end allows users to modify invoice amounts, impersonate other customer accounts, or execute unverified orders.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building a robust Telegram Mini App shop requires verifying the raw &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; payload using an HMAC-SHA256 signature on the server, calculating cart prices strictly from stored backend database values, controlling Telegram's native &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; across React render lifecycles, and accounting for renderer discrepancies between iOS WebViews and Telegram Desktop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Validating Telegram initData in Next.js Route Handlers
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a client triggers a checkout flow, the application must pass the raw &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initData&lt;/code&gt; query string to a Next.js App Router Route Handler (&lt;code&gt;app/api/checkout/route.ts&lt;/code&gt;). Never pass pre-parsed JSON objects from &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt;. The raw string contains key-value pairs sorted alphabetically and signed by Telegram using a secret key derived from your Bot Token.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your API route receives a list of product IDs and quantities, it must recalculate the total price on the server side using your application's product catalog. Once verified, the route calls Telegram's &lt;code&gt;createInvoiceLink&lt;/code&gt; Bot API endpoint to return a native payment link back to the front end.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is how to validate &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; and generate an invoice link securely in a Next.js Route Handler:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/api/checkout/route.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;next/server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CartItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PRODUCT_CATALOG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;priceInCents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;item_1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Developer Mug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;priceInCents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1500&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;item_2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Mechanical Keyboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;priceInCents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12000&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;verifyTelegramInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;initDataRaw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URLSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;initDataRaw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;isValid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;entries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckArray&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;sha256&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;WebAppData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;sha256&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;isValid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;parseInt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;auth_date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;floor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;86400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;isValid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Reject auth_date older than 24 hours&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userRaw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
